    "updated_at": "2026-06-10T10:59:23Z",
    "body": "> Why do we have these steps? They make nodes non-inert if _contextElement_'s node document is non-inert. This can cause images to load, for example.\n\nThat wording was introduced in https://github.com/WICG/sanitizer-api/pull/208. That was part of a larger re-write, so there is no justifcation for that specific section.\n\nFrom what I remember:\n* I'm fairly sure I didn't understand about inert-ness at the time, so whatever effect it has on inert is accidental (and maybe wrong). \n* We meanwhile changed the reference to the algorithm being called beforehand -- _HTML fragment parsing algorithm_ instead of _fragment parsing algorithm_.  I can no longer find a reference to the latter. I wonder if that had a different return type, and the idea was to convert them into a Node so we could call sanitize on it? \n\n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
